This Western blot (Figure 7D) confirms that Nano-11 induces the secretion of the active 17 kDa form of IL-1β, a key pro-inflammatory cytokine, particularly when dendritic cells are primed with LPS. While LPS alone (without Nano-11) leads to the production of inactive 30 kDa pro-IL-1β in the cell lysate, the presence of Nano-11 alongside LPS priming results in the cleavage of pro-IL-1β and the robust secretion of the active 17 kDa form into the supernatant, thus verifying the ELISA results shown in Figure 7C.